# UX copy

Follow `design-system/guidelines/ux-copy.md` before writing or editing any user-facing string.

- Accuracy > clarity > brevity > personality.
- Canonical terms: report, issue, issue type, location, photo, update, status, team, resolved, confirmed, reopen.
- Sentence case. No ALL-CAPS labels and no `text-transform: uppercase` on UI copy.
- Put reusable strings in `lib/i18n.ts`. Do not hardcode English or Hindi in components.
- Buttons are verb-led and name the object: “Submit report”, “Reopen report”.
- Errors = problem + recovery. Permissions = what + why + alternative.
- Do not invent SLAs, monitoring, or emergency coverage.
- If a simpler sentence says the same thing, use it.

```ts
// ❌
"Your grievance has been registered successfully"
"PHOTO EVIDENCE"
"View proof trail"

// ✅
"Report submitted"
"Photo"
"View report"
```
